<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Narasimha I (Hoysala)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1152–1173</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Narasimha I was king of the Hoysala dynasty from 1152 to 1173, the son and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishnuvardhana">Vishnuvardhana</a>. He inherited a large and wealthy kingdom but lacked his father's energy, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysalas</a> remained in the shadow of the Kalachuris who had seized the Western Chalukya capital Kalyani. He was overthrown by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veera-ballala-ii">Veera Ballala II</a>.</p></div>
